    "summary": "High‑energy set with stellar Samson→Terrapin→Truckin' medley",
    "blurb": "First set delivers tight renditions of 'Feel Like A Stranger', 'Peggy-O', and 'Bird Song'. The second set shines with a seamless Samson & Delilah → Terrapin Station → Truckin' flow into an explosive Smokestack Lightning jam and soulful Stella Blue. Overall show is strong despite a weak Day Job encore.",
    "review": "On March 10, 1985 at Berkeley Community Theater the Dead were firing on all cylinders. The first set opened with the crisp groove of 'Feel Like A Stranger' and kept momentum through 'Peggy-O', 'C.C. Rider' and a soaring 'Bird Song'. The second set is the highlight: 'Samson & Delilah' segues into an inspired 'Terrapin Station' that bursts into 'Truckin'', which then rolls straight into a blazing 'Smokestack Lightning' jam, complete with a tight pre‑drums improvisation that feeds into 'Space', a heartfelt 'Stella Blue', and the rousing sing‑along of 'Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad'. The band’s energy stays high through the closing 'Around & Around' and a rocking 'Johnny B. Goode', though the encore 'Keep Your Day Job' felt out of step with the rest of the night.",
